// =============================================================================
// Detection: Permission (consent) granted to an application
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform  (lab/ - ITDR pack)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   Any new delegated or application permission given to an app - the
//   illicit-consent / OAuth-phishing path, and the quiet way a compromised
//   admin hands an attacker's app tenant-wide Graph access. Three audit shapes:
//     "Consent to application"                     -> the consent itself (user
//                                                     or admin), ConsentContext.*
//     "Add delegated permission grant"             -> oauth2PermissionGrant
//                                                     created (also via Graph API)
//     "Add app role assignment to service principal" -> an APPLICATION
//                                                     permission (app-only, always
//                                                     tenant-wide) granted to an app
//   One admin consent writes several of these with the same CorrelationId;
//   they become separate alerts that Sentinel groups into one incident.
//
// SEVERITY (dynamic - the Severity column)
//   TenantWide = admin consent, consent on behalf of all users, or an
//                application permission.
//   HighRisk   = at least one permission on the HighRiskPermissions list (mail,
//                files - the scopes OAuth-phishing kits ask for - and every
//                Tier-0 Graph permission: directory/app/role write, PIM
//                schedules and policies, permission-grant and auth-method
//                policy, password profile, organization, entitlement mgmt).
//   High   : TenantWide AND HighRisk (an app can now read every mailbox or
//            rewrite the directory without any user present).
//   Medium : TenantWide OR HighRisk.
//   Low    : a low-risk single-user consent, or the CI apply identity.
//   Healthcare note: user consent should be OFF (admin consent workflow
//   only), which makes every row here a deliberate admin action.
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   AuditLogs, Category "ApplicationManagement". Permissions come from the
//   modifiedProperties ConsentAction.Permissions ("... Scope: Mail.Read
//   User.Read, ..."), DelegatedPermissionGrant.Scope and AppRole.Value.
//   verify: the exact modifiedProperty names for "Add delegated permission
//   grant" and "Add app role assignment to service principal" on the first
//   consent in the lab tenant (they match community rules, not a Microsoft
//   schema document).
//
// LICENSE
//   AuditLogs export to Log Analytics; no premium licence needed.
//
// MITRE ATT&CK
//   T1528 Steal Application Access Token (CredentialAccess)
//   T1098.003 Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Roles - app role grants
//   (Persistence, PrivilegeEscalation)
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - Onboarding a sanctioned SaaS app (admin consent, usually Medium). Tie it
//     to the change ticket; keep a short allow-list of approved client app
//     ids in a Sentinel watchlist if the volume ever needs it.
//   - The CI apply identity granting Graph roles to the pipeline apps (Low;
//     matched by its immutable ids - see IacPrincipalIds; an app merely NAMED
//     like it is High, IacNameSpoof).
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   Frequency 5m · Lookback 1h · one alert per row · Severity column ·
//   Entities: Account = ActorUpn / ActorObjectId, IP = ActorIp.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE
//   Notify on every incident; containment card on High (the CONSENTING
//   identity is the subject). Revoking the grant / disabling the app is an
//   app-owner decision and stays manual (runbook step): removing a grant can
//   break a sanctioned integration.
// =============================================================================

let LookBack = 1h;
// The CI apply identity, matched on IMMUTABLE ids (service principal object
// id / application client id), never on its display name: anyone who owns or
// administers an app can rename it "gh-oidc-entra-apply (write)", and a
// display-name match would DOWNGRADE that attacker's changes.
// modules/monitoring renders the list from var.iac_principal_ids (envs/
// bootstrap output iac_principal_ids). Committed, it is empty: run as-is,
// nothing counts as IaC - fail closed, severity can only go up.
let IacPrincipalIds = dynamic(["44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444"]); // @@IAC_PRINCIPAL_IDS@@
let IacDisplayName = "gh-oidc-entra-apply (write)"; // impersonation check ONLY, never trust
// Data-access scopes OAuth-phishing kits ask for, plus every Tier-0 Graph
// permission: one that lets an app make itself (or anyone) Global Admin, take
// over accounts or switch off the controls. Keep the Tier-0 part in step with
// Find-ShadowAdmins.ps1 / 06-NHI-Inventory.ps1 ($Tier0GraphPermissions).
let HighRiskPermissions = dynamic([
    "Mail.Read", "Mail.ReadWrite", "Mail.Send", "MailboxSettings.ReadWrite",
    "EWS.AccessAsUser.All", "full_access_as_app", "Contacts.Read",
    "Files.Read.All", "Files.ReadWrite.All", "Sites.Read.All", "Sites.ReadWrite.All",
    "Sites.FullControl.All", "Notes.Read.All",
    "Directory.ReadWrite.All", "Directory.AccessAsUser.All", "Application.ReadWrite.All",
    "AppRoleAssignment.ReadWrite.All", "RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory",
    "RoleAssignmentSchedule.ReadWrite.Directory", "RoleEligibilitySchedule.ReadWrite.Directory",
    "RoleManagementPolicy.ReadWrite.Directory",
    "PrivilegedAccess.ReadWrite.AzureADGroup", "PrivilegedAssignmentSchedule.ReadWrite.AzureADGroup",
    "PrivilegedEligibilitySchedule.ReadWrite.AzureADGroup",
    "User.ReadWrite.All", "User-PasswordProfile.ReadWrite.All", "Group.ReadWrite.All",
    "GroupMember.ReadWrite.All", "Policy.ReadWrite.ConditionalAccess",
    "Policy.ReadWrite.PermissionGrant", "Policy.ReadWrite.AuthenticationMethod",
    "UserAuthenticationMethod.ReadWrite.All", "Domain.ReadWrite.All",
    "Organization.ReadWrite.All", "EntitlementManagement.ReadWrite.All"]);
AuditLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(LookBack)
| where Category == "ApplicationManagement"
| where Result =~ "success"
| where OperationName in~ ("Consent to application", "Add delegated permission grant",
                           "Add app role assignment to service principal")
| extend ActorUpn      = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName)
| extend ActorObjectId = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.id)
| extend ActorApp      = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.displayName)
| extend ActorIp       = iff(isnotempty(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress)),
                             tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress),
                             tostring(InitiatedBy.app.ipAddress))
| extend Actor         = iff(isnotempty(ActorUpn), ActorUpn, ActorApp)
| mv-apply tr = TargetResources on (
    where tostring(tr.type) =~ "ServicePrincipal"
    | take 1
    | extend TargetName     = tostring(tr.displayName),
             TargetObjectId = tostring(tr.id),
             ModProps       = tr.modifiedProperties
  )
| mv-apply mp = ModProps on (
    summarize IsAdminConsentRaw = take_anyif(tostring(mp.newValue), tostring(mp.displayName) =~ "ConsentContext.IsAdminConsent"),
              OnBehalfOfAllRaw  = take_anyif(tostring(mp.newValue), tostring(mp.displayName) =~ "ConsentContext.OnBehalfOfAll"),
              PermissionsRaw    = take_anyif(tostring(mp.newValue), tostring(mp.displayName) =~ "ConsentAction.Permissions"),
              DelegatedScopeRaw = take_anyif(tostring(mp.newValue), tostring(mp.displayName) =~ "DelegatedPermissionGrant.Scope"),
              AppRoleValueRaw   = take_anyif(tostring(mp.newValue), tostring(mp.displayName) =~ "AppRole.Value"),
              ClientAppRaw      = take_anyif(tostring(mp.newValue), tostring(mp.displayName) =~ "ServicePrincipal.DisplayName")
  )
| extend GrantKind = case(
    OperationName =~ "Add app role assignment to service principal", "ApplicationPermission",
    OperationName =~ "Add delegated permission grant",               "DelegatedGrant",
    "Consent")
// "Consent to application" targets the CLIENT app; the other two target the
// RESOURCE (e.g. Microsoft Graph) and name the client in a modified property.
| extend ClientApp = iff(GrantKind == "Consent", TargetName, trim(@'"', ClientAppRaw))
| extend ResourceApp = iff(GrantKind == "Consent", "", TargetName)
| extend PermissionText = case(
    GrantKind == "Consent",        strcat_array(extract_all(@"Scope:\s*([^,\]]+)", PermissionsRaw), " "),
    GrantKind == "DelegatedGrant", trim(@'"', DelegatedScopeRaw),
    trim(@'"', AppRoleValueRaw))
// '-' is part of a permission name (User-PasswordProfile.ReadWrite.All);
// splitting on it would let a hyphenated Tier-0 scope slip past the list.
| extend Permissions = extract_all(@"([A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*)", PermissionText)
| extend HighRiskGranted = set_intersect(Permissions, HighRiskPermissions)
| extend IsAdminConsent = trim(@'"', IsAdminConsentRaw) =~ "True"
| extend OnBehalfOfAll  = trim(@'"', OnBehalfOfAllRaw) =~ "True"
| extend TenantWide = IsAdminConsent or OnBehalfOfAll or GrantKind == "ApplicationPermission"
| extend HighRisk   = array_length(HighRiskGranted) > 0
| extend ActorSpId  = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.servicePrincipalId)
| extend ActorAppId = tostring(InitiatedBy.app.appId)
| extend IsIac = (isnotempty(ActorSpId) and ActorSpId in (IacPrincipalIds))
              or (isnotempty(ActorAppId) and ActorAppId in (IacPrincipalIds))
// The IaC name on an app that is NOT the IaC identity = someone impersonating
// the pipeline to look routine. Always High.
| extend IacNameSpoof = not(IsIac) and ActorApp =~ IacDisplayName
| extend Severity = case(
    IacNameSpoof,            "High",
    IsIac,                   "Low",
    TenantWide and HighRisk, "High",
    TenantWide or HighRisk,  "Medium",
    "Low")
| project TimeGenerated, Severity, Actor, ActorUpn, ActorObjectId, ActorApp, ActorIp, IsIac, IacNameSpoof,
          OperationName, GrantKind, ClientApp, ResourceApp, TargetObjectId, IsAdminConsent,
          OnBehalfOfAll, TenantWide, Permissions, HighRiskGranted, CorrelationId
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
